WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.405
Messier 37 is the brightest and richest open cluster in the constellation Auriga.

00:05.856 --> 00:11.796
It was discovered by the Italian astronomer Giovanni Battista Hodierna before 1654.

00:12.234 --> 00:21.245
M37 was missed by French astronomer Guillaume Le Gentil when he rediscovered M36 and M38 in 1749.

00:21.773 --> 00:31.618
French astronomer Charles Messier independently rediscovered M37 in September 1764 but all three of these clusters were recorded by Hodierna.

00:32.198 --> 00:36.747
It is classified as Trumpler type I,1,r or I,2,r.
